      "writtenOn": "2023-01-09T17:51:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`SkTraceEventCommon.h` now only overrides tracing macros in Android framework when `SK_ANDROID_FRAMEWORK_USE_PERFETTO` is set, which only excludes host builds, where ATrace is a no-op anyway. This is to keep our number of separate cases where we override tracing macros differently to \"just\" three, instead of adding a fourth case (i.e. if we had separate cases for \"just ATrace\" vs. \"ATrace or Perfetto\". Instead we just have the \"ATrace or Perfetto\" case, since that\u0027s the only one that would be used in practice anyway).\n\nSo `SkTraceEventCommon.h` now only needs to `#include \u003ccutils/trace.h\u003e` when `SK_ANDROID_FRAMEWORK_USE_PERFETTO` is set, but this file still needs it to compile for `SK_BUILD_FOR_ANDROID_FRAMEWORK` in general.",
      "parentUuid": "98faec83_3fca21fd",
      "revId": "d5d19edfc5d61f6b1949fcd0f56439c61ac7071c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
