      "writtenOn": "2023-01-09T17:51:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The compile-time failure that I added will only check if `TRACE_EVENT_ATRACE_OR_PERFETTO_FORCEABLE` is used correctly (that it was given a category that ends with `.always` if `force_always_trace \u003d\u003d true`), but honestly that\u0027s sort of an internal implementation detail that\u0027s handled by `TRACE_EVENT0_ALWAYS`, which is what Skia developers should be calling.\n\nOtherwise the only other compile-time failures are:\n1. A non-always category entry must be present in this list for categories used in macros like `TRACE_EVENT0`.\n2. A `.always` category variant must be present in this list for categories used in `TRACE_EVENT0_ALWAYS`.\n\n(Those are both given to us for free by Perfetto)\n\nBut there\u0027s no cross-checking that the other one is present. How do you feel about this, and the approach of the comment saying \"you should probably add both, but you don\u0027t have to\"? Should we go with the \"you always have to add both\" approach instead?",
